=== what rung 5 does not carry over from APL ===

SKIP  v¨⍳9  out of scope: each over ⍳9 with an ARRAY operand makes a nine-element nested vector; a strand here is a tuple of two or three names, and nothing builds a tuple of nine
SKIP  f¨ over a strand, dyadically  out of scope: only the monadic form reads a name strand; a dyadic ¨ pairing two strands has no rule
SKIP  2f/v  out of scope: n-wise reduction is the derived function of / called dyadically, and a derived function is not a value here (rung 7)
SKIP  ⍺⍺ ⍵⍵  out of scope: a direct OPERATOR still takes its operands as names (rung 4's note stands)
SKIP  f⍣g with ⍵ as the old value  out of scope: the stop function is called with the new value as ⍺ and the old as ⍵, as in APL; a function that never fires is a contract violation after a million steps, not a hang
SKIP  a name strand  out of scope: it is built from a THIRD closed name set, not from every APL name: over all names two ordinary names on consecutive lines merge into one strand (v07_tuple)
SKIP  an all-uppercase name  out of scope: a word of two or more uppercase letters is a Fortress OPERATOR, so the program's BLK is written Blk (v06_caps)
